# One huge allocator per process: the run authorities `Huge::new` makes
# are the process's, as class::table's axiom_slot_loc for the slot ones.
axiom_run_locs	allocator invariant	none (assumption)
# Temporary seam: check_zero reads the run through the permission to
# its bytes, which the live-block model mints (a later PR).
Huge::check_zero	allocator invariant	Verus
# The zero tokens of a run `take` hands out (zero_run, their one caller,
# pinned by huge::tests::zero_axioms_called_from_zero_run_only): kernel
# zero-fill facts under the allocator's rules. zero_run's requires tie the
# fresh-page premise to the mark; the Purged premise, that
# purge::purged_is_zero read true, is not checked (a follow-up takes
# purge::purged_zero's PurgedZero witness, as the class claim path does).
axiom_fresh_anon_zero	allocator invariant	none (assumption)
axiom_discarded_zero	allocator invariant	none (assumption)
